959 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Strategic Influence\nConnected Experiences: Wrote the design strategy narrative for the newly formed org and co-authored its broader ecosystem vision for leadership reviews\nWindows Share: Co-authored the FY26 strategy with PM and helped shift the cross-device strategy to focus on how third-party apps work across devices.\nDrag and drop in Universal Composer: Co-led the proposal and leadership presentation that secured roadmap priority and a team to deliver drag-and-drop\nMicrosoft Store: Defined the vision for the developer experience and presented it in leadership reviews.)
/K [9]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 960 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
endobj
960 0 obj
<<
/K [959 0 R]
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
/P 941 0 R
>>
endobj
961 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Product Growth & Impact\nWindows Share: Led design across apps, people and devices, driving 6.2x growth in share completions \(18M to 112M\). Higher share completion is linked to higher Windows daily usage, making sharing a driver of platform engagement\nDrop Tray: Led design and launch of a new Windows drag-and-drop surface, contributing to 6x growth in completion sessions \(0.79M to 4.75M\) within a year of phased global rollout.)
/K [10]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 962 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
endobj
962 0 obj
<<
/K [961 0 R]
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
/P 941 0 R
>>
endobj
963 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (AI-Led Innovation\nDrag and drop in Universal Composer: Shaped how Windows suggests actions based on file content and system context. Designed simple actions and multi-step AI workflows, including Hold to collect files for later and hand-off to Copilot\nWindows Share: Led design of AI actions that help users tailor content and communicate better before sharing.\nSemantic Search: Created a UX framework for AI-powered search across File Explorer, Windows Search and Recall for a design leadership review.)
/K [11]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 964 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
endobj
964 0 obj
<<
/K [963 0 R]
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
/P 941 0 R
>>
endobj
965 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (0-to-1 Product Creation\nDrop Tray: Led design from concept to launch of a new Windows surface that brings relevant destinations to users when they start dragging a file.\nConnected Experiences: Led a Connected Intelligence sprint to explore new features that bring Windows and phones closer together, identifying opportunities for users to access content and continue tasks across devices.)
/K [12]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 966 0 R
/Pg 5 0 R
>>
